G73|overnight-reader-stops-after-first-book|~~closed=2026-03-14b~~
  was=overnight runner completes one book and exits; no queue advancement
  fix=claudecode/drain_learn_queue.py: loops learn_queue.json until empty; PID-guarded; 60s between launches; auto-spawned by learn_about() when items queued

G74|no-autonomous-source-discovery|open|ticket=#215
  was=topic→reading list requires manual URL curation; no TopicExpander
  fix=TopicExpander: anonymous browser_use to free AI web UI → parse URLs into LearningQueue; Calibre CSV as priority local source

G75|no-learning-queue-infrastructure|open|ticket=#215
  was=no persistent queue, no rate-limited fetcher, no blob→book_learner trigger, no overnight scheduler
  fix=LearningQueue (SQLite), ParallelFetcher (rate-limited per domain, parallel), NightlyRunner (cron, drains queue)

G-BRW2|ollama-external-ip|~~closed=2026-03-14g~~
  was=Ollama systemd service bound 127.0.0.1 only; cluster_status reported unreachable for local box
  fix=user added Environment="OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0" to /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/override.conf + daemon-reload + restart
  result=cluster_status can now reach Ollama via external IP

G-BRW3|inference-controller-auto-restart|~~closed=2026-03-14g~~
  was=Ollama failure required manual restart; inference_gateway.py had no recovery path
  fix=restart_ollama tool in cluster_ssh.py (local: sudo systemctl, remote: SSH+sudo; 5s wait + health check); _try_restart_local_ollama() in inference_gateway.py called when is_healthy()=False; 60s cooldown; always-on; logs OLLAMA_RESTART_OK/FAIL/ERROR
  result=Ollama auto-restarts within 60s of failure; manual tool available for remote machines

G-BRW4|browser-use-schema-compat|~~closed=2026-03-14g~~
  was=browser-use 0.11.9 generated minimum:0 on integer schema fields; Claude-sonnet-4-6 via Anthropic rejected HTTP 400 on every step; browser opened but never acted
  fix=upgraded browser-use 0.11.9→0.12.2; fixed result.final_state().url→result.urls()[-1] (API removed); switched LLM to gpt-4o-mini (cheaper, no schema strictness); BROWSER_USE_MODEL env var for override
  result=browser discovery working; Gemini navigated + typed prompt successfully

G-BRW5|topic-extraction-thread-context-pollution|open|small
  what=_extract_topic() used startswith(); CC bridge passes full thread context as user_input; trigger phrase in middle → whole blob returned as topic
  fix=changed to find() in learner.py; searches anywhere in input
  trigger=verify next session with "go learn about X" via CC bridge

G-BRW1|cc-bridge-greeting-dominance|open|small
  what=CC bridge messages fire PROC_GREETING instead of action habits for short requests
  why=PROC_GREETING scores too high at tier.2; action habits (PROC_GO_LEARN etc) don't compete
  fix=options: lower PROC_GREETING threshold for cc_bridge source; or route cc_bridge to tier.3+ directly
  trigger=whenever CC bridge is used for action requests

G-DBM1|memory-last-accessed-not-updated|open|small
  what=last_accessed=None on all memories including CPs; record_activation() only called on habit fires, never on search() results or interpretive traversal
  fix=update last_accessed on top-N memories surfaced into LLM context (search + interpretive BFS); lightweight batch write
  trigger=after slow query baseline confirmed via db_queries.log (avoid adding writes before knowing load)

